From 584cab4843f108321cddff85e3121ac82ce181e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Longwei Yang <19267252+Longwei-Yang@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:37:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 25/26] Safarium: Dock bounce for drawAttention; no caret
 browsing

- WebUIBrowserWindow::FlashFrame asks AppKit for a critical attention
  request (Dock icon bounces until Safarium is activated); views'
  NativeWidgetMac::FlashFrame is a stub, so Chrome itself never bounced.
  Reached by an extension's windows.update({drawAttention: true}).
- Caret browsing removed, as in Safari: no F7 shortcut, and the
  Settings > Accessibility toggle is hidden.
- The Mac window's command handling runs History > Reopen All Windows
  from Last Session (previous commit) and enables it only when
  safarium::CanReopenLastSession().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
